         text="Peisistratos drove into the Agora with his mules and himself wounded, claiming enemies had attacked him, and the assembly voted him a bodyguard of club-bearers. With them he took the Acropolis. Twice exiled, he came back for good in 546 and ruled until his death in 528, mildly by most accounts, building, holding festivals and lending money to farmers.",
