         text="During the Panathenaic procession two lovers, angered by an insult to Harmodios' sister, stabbed the tyrant's brother Hipparchos near the Leokoreion. Harmodios was killed on the spot, Aristogeiton tortured to death; Hippias ruled four more harsh years. Later Athenians made the pair heroes of freedom, with bronze statues in the Agora, though Thucydides insists the motive was personal.",
