         text="After the tyrants' fall Cleisthenes the Alkmeonid 'took the people into partnership'. He reorganised the citizens into ten new tribes mixing coast, plain and hills, founded on the demes, and created a council of 500 chosen by lot. When the Spartan king Kleomenes tried to undo it, the people besieged him on the Acropolis until he left. Democracy began here.",
