         text="The Athenians had abandoned the city for Salamis, leaving a few defenders behind wooden barricades on the Acropolis. Xerxes' men climbed the steep north side by the shrine of Aglauros, killed the defenders and burned the temples, the unfinished Parthenon and the statues. The Athenians later buried the broken korai on the rock, where they were found in the 1880s.",
