         text="After the first year of war the bones of the dead were carried in cypress coffins, one for each tribe, to the public cemetery outside the Dipylon. Pericles spoke from a high platform: 'We are a model to others rather than imitators', 'the whole earth is the tomb of famous men'. Thucydides wrote the speech as he remembered or reimagined it.",
