         text="With the country people packed inside the walls, a disease arrived from the east through Piraeus: fever, thirst, sores, delirium. Thucydides caught it and survived; he describes the dying lying in the temples and round the fountains, and funeral customs abandoned. Perhaps a quarter of the population died over three years, Pericles among them in 429.",
