         text="Hailed as a saviour god for driving out Cassander's garrison, the Macedonian prince Demetrius Poliorcetes was lodged by the flattering Athenians in the back room of the Parthenon, as 'younger brother' of Athena. Plutarch says he turned it into a brothel. A few years later the Athenians sang a hymn to him as a present god, unlike the others, who were far away or deaf.",
