         text="Attalos II of Pergamon, who had studied in Athens as a young man, paid for a two-storey marble stoa along the east side of the Agora, 115 m long with 42 shops. Its dedication was carved on the architrave. Hellenistic kings competed to adorn Athens, still the cultural capital of the Greek world though its power was gone.",
